course: dictionary
lesson: 4175
title: Words with a special meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have one meaning in a dictionary and a second, special meaning in a story, a religious ceremony or a joke. Godmother is one of them. In church life, a godmother is a woman who promises at a child's baptism or christening to help bring the child up in the Christian faith and to care for them. «khreshchEnyi and khreshchEna mean godfather and godmother; godparents are treated almost as family.» The sentence tells you that the relationship is close, almost like family.
explain: Context helps you choose the right meaning. Read the words around godmother. If the sentence mentions a christening, a baptism or a church, the church meaning fits. If it mentions a magic wand, a pumpkin coach or a ball, it is the fairy tale meaning, as in «Cinderella».
explain: The fairy tale meaning is a magic helper who appears when you need one. People also use it as a joke. «I need a fairy godmother» means I need someone to rescue me from a tricky spot. It does not mean you really expect a magic wand.
fact: Godmother means a woman who promises to help bring up a child in the Christian faith and care for them.
fact: A fairy godmother is a magic helper in fairy tales, such as the one in «Cinderella».
fact: «Godparents» are treated almost as family, but they are chosen for a special role at a christening.
fact: In a joke, «I need a fairy godmother» means you wish someone would help you out of trouble.
fact: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence and see whether it still makes sense.
exercise: Which sentence shows the church meaning of godmother? | A fairy who turns a pumpkin into a coach | *A woman who promises at a christening to help bring the child up and care for them | A helper who only appears in the middle of a film | A girl who lives next door
exercise: «At the ball, Cinderella's fairy godmother waved her wand.» What is a fairy godmother here? | A church leader who blesses babies | *A magic helper from a fairy tale | A kind neighbour who bakes cakes | A teacher who gives extra homework
exercise: Ruby says, «I need a fairy godmother to finish this maths test!» What does she mean? | She is sure a real magic helper is coming | *She wishes someone would help her out of a tricky spot | She is going to a christening | She wants to become a teacher
test: «Her godmother promised to care for her if anything happened.» What does this sentence show about a godmother? | She only gives presents at Christmas | She is a stranger who lives far away | *She is treated almost as family and helps care for the child
test: «khreshchEnyi and khreshchEna mean godfather and godmother.» Which word is the male version of godmother? | *godfather | godchild | godson
exam: Read this: «My godmother helped me choose my school, and she always sends a card on my birthday.» What does godmother mean here? | A teacher at the church | A magic fairy with a wand | *A woman who promises to help bring me up and care for me | A bridesmaid at a wedding
